I am outlining upload requirements for exams and penalties for non-complian=
ce effective from Exam 1A onwards. All those who violate these requirements=
 are penalized and are notified by means of a comment attached to the exam;=
 such students should read the comments and do as instructed if they wish n=
ot to be penalized in the future. Students MUST inspect their documents to =
ensure that ALL these requirements are indeed met. If one does not have a g=
ood scanner, one is free to use the ones at CCP. One should be very wise to=
 scan something and send it to oneself to make sure that one is using the s=
canner properly. One has the option of discussing the matter on DISCORD and=
 get help from those who are doing things correctly because there are many =
of these.



ONE MUST CHECK ONE'S SUBMISSION TO ENSURE THAT THESE CONDITIONS ARE MET.



(0) SINGLE DOCUMENT



There should be a SINGLE, PROPERLY ORIENTED, SUFFICIENTLY WELL-LIT, LEGIBLE=
 document. Penalty for non-compliance: 0 on the Exam.



(1) DOCUMENT SIZE < 25 MB



The document should be LESS THAN 25 MB IN SIZE because otherwise there is a=
 crash warning which I am not ready to ignore. This is achieved by reducing=
 the resolution for the scanned document. Proper size may be achieved in ma=
ny ways and one is well-advised to watch youtube videos to see how this is =
done. Penalty for non-compliance: 0 on the Exam.



(2) LEGIBLE DOCUMENT



Illegible documents arise when one is scanning in a dimly lit location; the=
refore one MUST USE SUFFICIENT LIGHTING WHILE SCANNING. It arises if one ha=
s poor handwriting and, in this case, one is well-advised to use appropriat=
e SOFTWARE THAT CAN PRODUCE ALL SYMBOLS REQUIRED. It also arises when one i=
s using pencils with lead that is too hard and thin. One should use lead of=
 DIAMETER GREATER THAN OR EQUAL TO .7mm and of SOFTNESS 2B, 3B, 4B OR HIGHE=
R. One should refer to ARTICLE 20 AND ITS PARTTS IN THE GENERAL INFORMATION=
 PACKET. Penalty for non-compliance: Half the number of points secured on t=
he exam.

