<p><strong>I am outlining upload requirements for exams and penalties for n=
on-compliance effective from Exam 1A onward</strong>s. All those who violat=
e these requirements are penalized and are notified by means of a comment a=
ttached to the exam; such students
 should read the comments and do as instructed if they wish not to be penal=
ized in the future. Students MUST inspect their documents to ensure that AL=
L these requirements are indeed met. If one does not have a good scanner, o=
ne is free to use the ones at CCP.
 One should be very wise to scan something and send it to oneself to make s=
ure that one is using the scanner properly. One has the option of discussin=
g the matter on DISCORD and get help from those who are doing things correc=
tly because there are many of these.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span><strong>ONE MUST CHECK ONE'S SUBMISSION TO ENSURE THAT THESE CONDI=
TIONS ARE MET</strong></span>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>(0)<span>&nbsp;</span><span>SINGLE DOCUMENT</span></strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>There should be a<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>SINGLE, PROPERLY ORIENTED, S=
UFFICIENTLY WELL-LIT, LEGIBLE</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>document.<span>&nb=
sp;</span><strong>Penalty for non-compliance: 0 on the Exam</strong>.&nbsp;=
</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>(1)<span>&nbsp;</span><span>DOCUMENT SIZE &lt; 25 MB</span></str=
ong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The document should be<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>LESS THAN 25 MB IN SIZE=
</strong>&nbsp;because otherwise there is a crash warning which I am not re=
ady to ignore. This is achieved by reducing the resolution for the scanned =
document. Proper size may be achieved in many
 ways and one is well-advised to watch youtube videos to see how this is do=
ne.<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>Penalty for non-compliance: 0 on the Exam</st=
rong>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>(2)<span>&nbsp;</span><span>LEGIBLE DOCUMENT</span></strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Illegible documents arise when one is scanning in a dimly lit location; =
therefore one<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>MUST USE</strong><span>&nbsp;</span=
><strong>SUFFICIENT LIGHTING WHILE SCANNING</strong>. It arises if one has =
poor handwriting and, in this case, one is
 well-advised to use appropriate<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>SOFTWARE THAT CA=
N PRODUCE ALL SYMBOLS REQUIRED</strong>. It also arises when one is using p=
encils with lead that is too hard and thin. One should use lead of<span>&nb=
sp;</span><strong>DIAMETER GREATER THAN OR
 EQUAL TO .7mm and of SOFTNESS 2B, 3B, 4B OR HIGHER</strong>. One should re=
fer to<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>ARTICLE 20 AND ITS PARTTS IN THE GENERAL I=
NFORMATION PACKET</strong>.<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>Penalty for non-compl=
iance: Half the number of points secured on
 the exam.</strong></p>
